    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Vinnie Pasquantino** serves as our anchor with the highest efficiency score of 72.87. He draws a favorable matchup against Barnett, where a soft SP_xERA of 4.56 and a significant +14% boost from platoon splits make him a lock in the 1B slot. **Corbin Carroll** remains a vital piece of the lineup despite the 30% rain risk; his score of 68.92 is heavily buoyed by an expected #2 spot in the order (+8%) and the need to capitalize on his elite speed to hunt stolen bases, even with a neutral matchup against Gamboa. Similarly, **Austin Riley** is a strong play at 65.33; while his #8 order position drags his score down, the combination of a high SP_xERA (4.81) and a slow delivery from Ober provides an excellent environment for him to generate production despite the lower lineup protection.\n\nThe decision to slot **Zach McKinstry** into the 2B spot was the narrowest call of the day. With a score of 49.68, he sits right on the edge of our \"Marginal\" threshold. He was selected over the rest of the bench\u2014which is largely compromised by off-days for **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor**, or injury status for **James Wood** and **Mickey Moniak**\u2014due to the mathematical necessity of filling the position against Mlodzinski. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention; while his 62.20 score is respectable, the matchup against Luis Castillo is capped by a -2% penalty due to the pitcher\u2019s ability to hold runners, slightly tempering his ceiling. We are keeping a close watch on **Gabriel Moreno**; while his 57.83 score is solid, the lingering 30% rain risk and the pending confirmation of his #3 spot require active monitoring to ensure he isn't a late scratch that could force a bench pivot.",
